1799		square root of the deficit
1800		\[
1801			1 - \E_{(\ell,\ell_X,\ell_Z) \sim D}\
1802			\E_{(x,z,\alpha,\beta) \in \ell} \sum_{a}
1803			\bra{\hat\psi}
1804			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z,x}_{a} \ot
1805			\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a}
1806			\ket{\hat\psi}\,,
1807			\qquad
1808			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z,x}_{a}
1809			= \sum_{f_X,f_Z \,:\, f_X(x)=a}
1810			T^{\ell_X,\ell_Z}_{f_X,f_Z}\,.
1811		\]
1812		By the sandwich definition of $T$ and the projectivity of the lines
1813		measurement $\{\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{f_X}\}$, the
1814		subtracted expectation equals
1815		$\E \sum_a \bra{\hat\psi}
1816		\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Line},X),\ell_X}_{[\mathrm{eval}_x(\cdot)=a]} \ot
1817		\hat{M}^{(\mathrm{Point},X),x}_{a} \ket{\hat\psi}$,
1818		which by Property~2 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-sublines} is a mixture of the
1819		corresponding averages over the restricted distributions
1820		$D_{\mathrm{v},i}$. By the error inflation of
1821		Lemma~\ref{lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds} applied to the
1822		line--point consistency in item~3 of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-comm-line-cons},
1823		each restricted term has deficit $O(m\,\delta_{\mathrm{Line}})$, so the
1824		total deficit is $O(m^2\,\delta_{\mathrm{Line}})$ (the final line of the
1825		source proof asserts this bound for the consistency term itself rather
1826		than for its deficit; see Remark~\ref{rem:qld-4-13-source-defects}).
1827		Taking the square root gives the claimed error
1828		$m\,\delta_{\mathrm{Line}}^{1/2}$.
